# What differs from run to run of the greenplum suite's ORCA pass with the
# same settings (differential.py): a regular expression a line, its groups
# replaced.
#
# a segment's next OID once a table is made and dropped: whatever else its
# backends allocated meanwhile (seen with vexec off, in off-again)
@oid_wraparound ^ +429000000(\d)$
# covar_pop over filter_test's nine rows in one stage, on the coordinator,
# where vexec's prices put it: the rows are summed as they arrive from the
# segments, and the last digits vary from run to run -- as they do with
# vexec off when ORCA plans that one stage -- with the header's padding and
# the rule's width
@filter ^ 2\.08163265306122(\d*)$
@filter ^( +)covar_pop( +)$
@filter ^(-{19,20})$
